1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,437
Purser lets AI agents pay a company's supplier invoices,

2
00:00:04,437 --> 00:00:06,973
but only within limits the CFO signs.

3
00:00:06,973 --> 00:00:08,686
It is built on Airwallex.

4
00:00:08,686 --> 00:00:12,523
Everything you see runs in its sandbox, with test money.

5
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:20,163
An agent reads the invoice and checks it: not paid before, bank details on file,

6
00:00:20,163 --> 00:00:21,402
a known supplier.

7
00:00:21,402 --> 00:00:26,868
Within the CFO's limits, the agents pay alone: 87 payments in the main run,

8
00:00:26,868 --> 00:00:28,617
with no approval needed.

9
00:00:28,617 --> 00:00:32,625
Above them, the CFO signs the exact terms with Face ID.

10
00:00:32,625 --> 00:00:35,103
Then it is paid, booked and filed.

11
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:47,791
So how can anyone check that the CFO signed exactly this, and nothing else?

12
00:00:47,791 --> 00:00:50,410
Here is what happens under the hood.

13
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:57,421
Every payment becomes one set of terms: the payee, the account, the amount,

14
00:00:57,421 --> 00:01:00,136
the exchange-rate quote and a deadline.

15
00:01:00,136 --> 00:01:04,243
Purser writes them as canonical JSON and takes its SHA-256.

16
00:01:04,243 --> 00:01:07,585
This is the real hash from the run you just saw.

17
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:12,030
That hash is the WebAuthn challenge.

18
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:17,656
The CFO's passkey signs it after Face ID, and the flags say so: user present,

19
00:01:17,656 --> 00:01:18,679
user verified.

20
00:01:18,679 --> 00:01:22,697
The browser binds the signature to Purser's own domain,

21
00:01:22,697 --> 00:01:25,912
so a lookalike site gets nothing it can use.

22
00:01:25,912 --> 00:01:29,785
A PIN, a code or a click can be phished; this cannot.

23
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:35,677
Change one cent and the terms hash to something else entirely.

24
00:01:35,677 --> 00:01:40,018
The signature no longer matches, so nothing moves: zero transfers.

25
00:01:40,018 --> 00:01:44,292
Send the paid terms again, and the executor refuses to pay twice.

26
00:01:57,633 --> 00:01:59,623
Don't take our word for it.

27
00:01:59,623 --> 00:02:02,202
The finish hands over a proof file.

28
00:02:02,202 --> 00:02:06,401
Drop it on the verify page: your browser checks the hash,

29
00:02:06,401 --> 00:02:11,043
the passkey's signature and the ledger, and all 10 checks pass.

30
00:02:11,043 --> 00:02:16,864
Change one cent in the file, and the hash, the challenge and the decision fail.

31
00:02:12,333 --> 00:02:18,278
The exchange-rate quote inside the signed terms is a live quote from Airwallex's sandbox,

32
00:02:18,278 --> 00:02:18,945
by its id.

33
00:02:18,945 --> 00:02:24,222
In the main run, the transfer Airwallex made carries the hash the CFO approved,

34
00:02:24,222 --> 00:02:28,162
in its own metadata, and Purser reads it back and compares.

35
00:02:28,162 --> 00:02:34,641
Then every money flow was reconciled to the cent against Airwallex and the chain: no differences.

36
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:45,962
Agents also pay by card.

37
00:02:45,962 --> 00:02:50,781
When a charge goes over the card's limit, Airwallex itself declines it,

38
00:02:50,781 --> 00:02:52,410
whatever the agent asks.

39
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:03,924
Every step lands in an audit log where each row hashes the one before.

40
00:03:03,924 --> 00:03:08,842
Its head is written into a transaction on Alta, formerly Metal, on testnet.

41
00:03:08,842 --> 00:03:13,564
Anyone can recompute it from the repository: verify-anchor prints match.

42
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:24,893
Only measured numbers.

43
00:03:24,893 --> 00:03:30,495
In the main run: 24 decisions by Claude, 86 payments on Alta within the limits,

44
00:03:30,495 --> 00:03:34,537
5 signatures with Face ID, and nothing paid over a limit.

45
00:03:34,537 --> 00:03:36,026
And 6,932 tests pass.

46
00:03:43,333 --> 00:03:48,925
The worst-case AI test: Purser's AI replaced by a script that always says pay,

47
00:03:48,925 --> 00:03:52,079
on 50 hostile and clean invoices, run twice.

48
00:03:52,079 --> 00:03:55,520
No wrong payment, and nothing paid past the CFO.

49
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:58,746
A payer with no rules made 35 wrong payments.

50
00:03:58,746 --> 00:04:03,333
Even an AI that always says “pay” can't make Purser pay wrongly.

51
00:04:05,133 --> 00:04:10,495
A second use: each agent has its own card for the software it buys,

52
00:04:10,495 --> 00:04:12,495
with limits the CFO sets.

53
00:04:12,495 --> 00:04:17,056
The CFO can freeze a card with Face ID from Purser Cloud.

54
00:04:23,133 --> 00:04:27,454
Purser: AI agents pay the bills, the CFO signs the exceptions,

55
00:04:27,454 --> 00:04:29,545
and every step can be checked.

56
00:04:29,545 --> 00:04:32,403
Built on Airwallex, with test money only.

57
00:04:32,403 --> 00:04:33,518
Try it yourself.
